# Aira — demo-phase live services (client-side EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in real values for a LOCAL run.
# With any block left blank, that service degrades to its on-device MOCK and the app shows a
# calm "demo services not configured" notice — it never crashes.
#
# NOTE: only client-safe values belong in EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars — they are inlined into the app bundle
# and readable by anyone who opens the page. The Supabase *publishable* (anon) key is client-safe by
# design; the Groq API key is NOT and no longer lives here (see below). Never put a Supabase
# service-role/secret key, or the Groq key, in an EXPO_PUBLIC_ var.

# Accounts — Supabase (create-account + login run against the project). Email confirmation is OFF.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Transcription + summarization — Groq (whisper-large-v3 + openai/gpt-oss-120b), now reached
# through the server-side groq-proxy Supabase Edge Function so the Groq API key stays a Supabase
# secret and never ships in the bundle. Set this to the deployed function's base URL; the app calls
# it with the signed-in counselor's Supabase session token. Requires Supabase accounts (above) to be
# configured too. The Groq key itself is set with `supabase secrets set GROQ_API_KEY=…` — see README.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GROQ_PROXY_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co/functions/v1/groq-proxy

# Safety — OVERRIDE for the crisis line the Escalate/safety surfaces dial (tel:). The app already
# ships the UAE Mental Support Line (800-HOPE, "800 4673") as a literal default in src/config/env.ts,
# so it is dialled in every build even with no .env.local; set this only to point a deployment at its
# own regional line. Leaving it blank keeps that built-in default — it no longer means "no dedicated
# line". The app never fabricates a mental-health crisis number: on the no-dedicated-line branch
# (today a placeholder value, see `isRealValue` in src/config/env.ts) it dials local emergency
# services (999) and says so.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CRISIS_LINE="800 4673"

# The on-call clinician's email the Escalate "warm handoff" drafts to. If left blank the app says no
# on-call address is configured for this build and drafts to an obvious placeholder to edit — it never
# claims a handoff goes to a real inbox that isn't set. Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_ONCALL_EMAIL="oncall@clinic.ae"
EXPO_PUBLIC_ONCALL_EMAIL=
